{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/499051-the-clockwork-nirvana-of-mechanus","id":499051,"title":"The Clockwork Nirvana of Mechanus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T10:11:50-07:00","id":499051,"title":"The Clockwork Nirvana of Mechanus","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanus\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Dados_4_a_20_caras_trans.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanus\" target=\"_blank\"> Outer Plane - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanus\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanus </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's a plane from the D&amp;D universe. Its inhabitants, the Inevitables, are much like angels, I noticed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inevitable_%28Dungeons_%26_Dragons%29\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Dados_4_a_20_caras_trans.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inevitable_%28Dungeons_%26_Dragons%29\" target=\"_blank\"> Outer Plane - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inevitable_%28Dungeons_%26_Dragons%29\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inevitable_%28Dungeons_%26_Dragons%29 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot; Every type of inevitable is designed to enforce a particular type of universal law and will pursue its objective at any cost. In order to fulfill their tasks, they may ally themselves with other creatures or, if necessary, sacrifice themselves.&quot;<br /> <br /> I thought maybe someone could work on Mechanus to make it the home of DtD angels, as some kind of story hook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:20:21-07:00","id":499079,"title":"","content":"Inevitables?<br /> <br /> Phah, try <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modron_%28Dungeons_%26_Dragons%29\" target=\"_blank\">Modrons</a> on for size.<br /> <br /> Primus is the God Machine.<br /> <br /> (OK, fine, Inevitables are <i>superficially</i> more angel-like, but they are the most &quot;normal&quot; of Mechanus' inhabitants.)<br /> <br /> Damn, now I want to play a game in the Great Wheel, but with NWoD. Shouldn't be <i>that</i> hard of a shard to come up with, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 05-01-2015, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:32:03-07:00","id":499099,"title":"","content":"Hey what if Inevitables could fall? :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:00:50-07:00","id":499127,"title":"","content":"Why do we need Inevitables to fall? They already have free will, it's just that they are created to uphold certain laws.<br /> <br /> Modrons, on the other hand, <i>can</i> fall, and the response to a rogue Modron mirrors the God-Machine's response to Demons. Angels are <i>basically</i> non-geometric Modrons. (I didn't just link them for my health, ya know.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T00:02:06-07:00","id":499929,"title":"","content":"Oh that page about Modrons is great!<br /> <br /> Now I can picture a Heirarch Modron as a fairly palpable antagonist in a Demon story, an Angel with a dictated role of being the governor of the God-Machine's plans over a specific city... Seems like they'd make a great recurring villian if done right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:37:03-07:00","id":500850,"title":"","content":"And each Time this angel fails they come a step closed to falling. If they fall well, they may either become an ally or a greater foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:21:11-07:00","id":501428,"title":"","content":"There is some good story potential there, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpa